  "summary_md": "Strategic portfolio reshaping defines today’s batch, with multiple companies exiting low-return segments and pivoting toward defense, AI infrastructure, and higher-margin applications. BWEN’s exit from wind towers, CMTL’s satellite divestiture, and TAYD’s transformation into a defense-aerospace pure-play exemplify the shift, while LASE and LTRX are leveraging military and unmanned systems demand. AI infrastructure tailwinds lift OCC and PKOH, though lumpy order patterns keep execution uneven. A parallel theme is the financial divide: cash-rich names like NTGR, BKTI, and RR deploy buybacks, whereas CETY and CLRO resort to distressed, dilutive capital raises. Management credibility remains the key variable as ambitious turnarounds at INSG and LTRX await tangible proof, and several restructurings (CVV, PKOH’s steel review) need to demonstrate that portfolio focus translates into sustained profitability.",
